1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,543
This is a developer walkthrough of the Razorpay UPI AutoPay integration.

2
00:00:05,543 --> 00:00:16,971
We will cover the architecture, how webhooks are handled, how payments and credits are protected from duplication, what is tested, and how to roll it out.

3
00:00:18,071 --> 00:00:20,407
Four rules shaped the design.

4
00:00:20,407 --> 00:00:26,288
Razorpay debits the customer, and nothing of ours ever initiates a debit.

5
00:00:26,288 --> 00:00:35,632
The browser proves nothing: plan access and credits follow a signed webhook or Razorpay's own API, never a redirect.

6
00:00:35,632 --> 00:00:41,110
The existing wallet ledger is reused, so there is no second balance.

7
00:00:41,110 --> 00:00:44,332
And the whole feature is off by default.

8
00:00:45,432 --> 00:00:47,170
Here is the shape of it.

9
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:58,250
A tenant request goes from the billing screen through a thin controller to the AutoPay service, and from there through the gateway interface to Razorpay.

10
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:00,785
The other direction is the webhook.

11
00:01:00,785 --> 00:01:08,534
The endpoint verifies and stores the event, a Hangfire job picks it up, and the event processor applies it.

12
00:01:08,534 --> 00:01:19,180
What a payment means for the tenant is kept apart, in AutoPay entitlements: the payment record, the plan period, the wallet credits and the notice.

13
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:24,141
The data model adds two tables and extends three.

14
00:01:24,141 --> 00:01:30,681
Razorpay plans are immutable, so one row maps each exact charge to a Razorpay plan.

15
00:01:30,681 --> 00:01:34,778
Each mandate attempt is a row that is never deleted.

16
00:01:34,778 --> 00:01:40,136
The existing subscription row points at the mandate behind the plan.

17
00:01:40,136 --> 00:01:45,258
Payments gain the gateway's ids and a succeeded or failed status.

18
00:01:45,258 --> 00:01:50,301
Webhook events keep their whole payload and a processing status.

19
00:01:50,301 --> 00:01:53,452
No UPI id, PIN or bank detail is stored.

20
00:01:54,552 --> 00:01:57,056
Checkout accepts only a plan id.

21
00:01:57,056 --> 00:02:03,392
The amount is worked out on the server from the country price plus tax, in paise.

22
00:02:03,392 --> 00:02:13,092
A free plan, a tenant not billed in rupees, or a price over the UPI limit is refused before anything is created at Razorpay.

23
00:02:13,092 --> 00:02:17,082
Any open mandate is checked against Razorpay first.

24
00:02:17,082 --> 00:02:24,278
A running one blocks the checkout, and a waiting one for the same amount is simply returned.

25
00:02:24,278 --> 00:02:29,441
Only then is the plan created, if it is new, and the subscription.

26
00:02:30,541 --> 00:02:38,331
The webhook endpoint reads the raw bytes and verifies the HMAC signature with a constant time comparison.

27
00:02:38,331 --> 00:02:48,346
It de-duplicates on the event id with a unique index, stores the whole payload as received, and only then answers 200 and queues a job.

28
00:02:48,346 --> 00:02:55,097
Nothing is applied inside the request, so a failure while applying can never lose an event.

29
00:02:56,197 --> 00:03:01,747
Razorpay does not guarantee order, so the processor does not assume it.

30
00:03:01,747 --> 00:03:08,000
Every subscription event carries the whole subscription as it stood when raised.

31
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,657
A newer event is applied as it is.

32
00:03:10,657 --> 00:03:17,692
An older one, or one from the same second, is not trusted, and Razorpay is asked directly.

33
00:03:17,692 --> 00:03:20,740
An ended mandate is never brought back.

34
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:26,837
And a charge that arrives late is still recorded, because the money was taken.

35
00:03:27,937 --> 00:03:35,799
Duplicates are stopped at four independent layers, all in the database or the ledger rather than in memory.

36
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:37,489
The event id is unique.

37
00:03:37,489 --> 00:03:41,017
An event already applied is never applied again.

38
00:03:41,017 --> 00:03:52,847
The payment table has a unique index on provider and payment id, so the same payment through two events, two workers, or the reconciliation job is still one row.

39
00:03:52,847 --> 00:03:58,873
And the ledger grants each operation key once, built from the Razorpay payment id.

40
00:03:58,873 --> 00:04:05,780
The payment and the plan change are saved together, and the credits follow, safely repeatable.

41
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:09,403
This table summarises the events.

42
00:04:09,403 --> 00:04:16,131
Authenticated and activated change only the mandate, because a mandate is not a payment.

43
00:04:16,131 --> 00:04:24,159
A charged event records the payment, extends the paid period, adds the credits once and tells the tenant.

44
00:04:24,159 --> 00:04:28,517
Pending leaves the plan alone and applies the grace days.

45
00:04:28,517 --> 00:04:30,888
Halted marks the plan past due.

46
00:04:30,888 --> 00:04:33,487
Cancelled keeps what was paid for.

47
00:04:33,487 --> 00:04:41,974
And a failed payment is recorded with its reason, matched to the mandate through its invoice, and adds nothing.

48
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:44,819
Four jobs support this.

49
00:04:44,819 --> 00:04:47,931
The webhook job applies one stored event.

50
00:04:47,931 --> 00:05:00,529
A retry pass every five minutes applies events that no job picked up, and failed events when they are due, with a wait that doubles up to six hours, for ten attempts.

51
00:05:00,529 --> 00:05:09,181
A daily reconciliation compares every live mandate with Razorpay, and recovers a missed payment from its invoices.

52
00:05:09,181 --> 00:05:13,962
And an hourly pass ends plans whose mandate has stopped paying.

53
00:05:13,962 --> 00:05:16,466
None of them ever starts a debit.

54
00:05:17,566 --> 00:05:26,800
On the screen, Subscribe sends only the plan id and opens Razorpay in a new tab, so the billing page stays where it is.

55
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:36,267
While the mandate is waiting, the page asks the server every five seconds for three minutes, and the server asks Razorpay.

56
00:05:36,267 --> 00:05:39,681
Active appears only when the server says so.

57
00:05:39,681 --> 00:05:42,941
After that, a Check status button remains.

58
00:05:42,941 --> 00:05:47,131
Plan buttons are disabled while a mandate is charging.

59
00:05:48,231 --> 00:06:02,380
There are two thousand eight hundred and one backend tests, one hundred and ninety seven of them new, and one thousand five hundred and ninety three screen tests, thirty two new.

60
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:08,103
They cover duplicates, races, out of order events, failures and retries.

61
00:06:08,103 --> 00:06:11,044
But there are zero calls to Razorpay.

62
00:06:11,044 --> 00:06:18,675
A fake plays Razorpay, with real services, the real ledger and a relational database underneath.

63
00:06:18,675 --> 00:06:22,490
Two workers racing was exercised only on SQLite.

64
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:26,239
For rollout, deploy the API first.

65
00:06:26,239 --> 00:06:30,758
The migration applies at start-up and nothing changes yet.

66
00:06:30,758 --> 00:06:32,940
Then deploy the Angular app.

67
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:43,770
Configure Razorpay in test mode with the keys and the webhook, run the thirteen step manual checklist, and only then switch the feature on.

68
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:46,575
Go live with one small real mandate.

69
00:06:46,575 --> 00:06:49,535
To roll back, set the switch to false.

70
00:06:49,535 --> 00:06:54,989
Existing mandates keep running and their webhooks are still processed.

71
00:06:56,089 --> 00:06:58,570
Finally, what is not yet known.

72
00:06:58,570 --> 00:07:10,494
We still need to see real UPI webhook payloads, to confirm which events arrive and in what order, and that a failed payment always names its invoice.

73
00:07:10,494 --> 00:07:18,417
The account needs Subscriptions and UPI enabled, and cancel at cycle end must be confirmed for UPI.

74
00:07:18,417 --> 00:07:26,179
Refunds, credit pack payments, pause from the app and switching between paid plans are not built.

75
00:07:26,179 --> 00:07:30,821
Two decisions remain: the grace days, and the GST invoice.

76
00:07:30,821 --> 00:07:34,822
All of this is written up in the documents folder.

77
00:07:34,822 --> 00:07:35,622
Thank you.

